# A parameter body inference ALREADY calls gen, fed a boxed argument — and the
# numeric pin demoting it, in a program with no other widening.
#
# THIS FIXTURE MUST STAY SMALL, and that is its whole design. The defect was
# invisible in a larger file: `widen_ptypes` is a fixpoint that stops when a
# round changes nothing, so any OTHER widening anywhere in the program buys a
# second round in which the demoted parameter is re-widened and re-recorded,
# and the bug disappears. Adding this case to t102 — which is full of
# widenings — would have gated nothing. Correctness must not depend on an
# unrelated part of the program existing, so the fixture must not supply one.
#
# The shape: `find_gen_param_use` classifies `n` gen on its own, because
# `takes_dict of n` puts it at a dict position. widen_scan's consult was gated
# on the parameter currently being `num`, so an already-gen parameter recorded
# no evidence — and the pin, which asks only what the body computes with
# (`n * 2`), demoted it to a C double. The backstop then refused the build:
#
#   VM   10 / 7 / guarded3-null    rc 0
#   AOT  build FAILS, no binary, "'shout' has no return statement ..."
#
# A straight regression: the previous commit compiled this correctly.

define takes_dict(d) as:
    if d != null:
        print of d.k

define shout(m) as:
    print of (m * 1)

define guarded3(n) as:
    if n == null:
        takes_dict of n
        print of "guarded3-null"
    else:
        print of (n * 2)

guarded3 of 5
guarded3 of (shout of 7)
